       characteristics:'Pure witnessing consciousness. Not inward, not outward, not between. Cannot be experienced as an object — it IS the experiencer. When "found," it is recognized as what was always already present.',
       science:'No EEG signature — because it is not a brain state. It is what observes brain states. Some researchers map it to gamma-band synchrony (40Hz+) in experienced meditators, but this is the brain\'s correlate, not the thing itself.',
       practice:'Every meditation practice ultimately points here. The question "Who is meditating?" — followed to its source — is the direct path. Ramana Maharshi\'s entire teaching: "Find the I-thought\'s source."',
       source:'Mandukya Upanishad 7; Mandukya Karika (Gaudapada); Yoga Sutras 1.3',
