    tag:'Experience',
    title:'Matsya — The Great Flood (Era 9)',
    body:`<em>The biggest single build on the site so far.</em> Nine acts. The viewer taps a small fish that grows through six vessel-sizes until no ocean can hold it. Shankhāsura rises from the deep and drags twelve Vedic syllables down into the abyss. Rain, lightning, waves eating the canvas. Manu's boat appears with <strong>all seven Saptarishis on deck</strong> — each glowing with their chakra color from Era 8. You drag to steer past floating debris of drowned civilizations. Matsya dives to Pātāla, fights the demon underwater with bioluminescence and writhing tentacles, and one by one the syllables rise back to the surface.<br><br>Ends at <em>Satyameva Jayate</em>.<br><br>The teaching under the myth: the flood is not about weather. It is about how truth survives chaos. Every civilization eventually drowns in its own noise. What makes it through — the Vedas, the Seers, the seeds of life — survives because consciousness itself guards it. -RR`
