    body:`Eras shipped so far: Brahman, Spanda, N\u0101da Brahma (1\u20133). \u015aiva\u2013\u015aakti (4). Hira\u1e47yagarbha (5). Vir\u0101\u1e6d (6). Kalpa (7). Sv\u0101yambhuva Manvantara (8). Matsya (9). K\u016brma\u2019s Samudra Manthan (10\u2019s sub-experience). Vaivasvata Manvantara (11). Narasi\u1e43ha (13). That\'s ten full era experiences plus the foundational metaphysics. <em>Today\'s Narasi\u1e43ha was the one I was nervous about. The next one is no longer scheduled \u2014 I\'ll wait until I know which one is asking to be written.</em><br><br>Still ahead: <strong>Era 10 K\u016brma proper</strong> (the tortoise as stable foundation \u2014 tectonic time, the psychology of groundedness, the Earth as living platform). <strong>Era 12 Var\u0101ha</strong> (the cosmic boar who lifts the Earth from the deep waters; rescue through strength and humility). <strong>Era 14 V\u0101mana</strong> (the dwarf who measured the cosmos in three steps; geometry of cosmic scale). <strong>Era 15 Para\u015bur\u0101ma</strong> (the warrior-sage; sacred anger when no other corrective remains). <strong>Era 16 R\u0101ma</strong> (Mary\u0101d\u0101 Puru\u1e63ottama; dharma as limit; the Yoga V\u0101si\u1e63\u1e6dha key). <strong>Eras 17\u201324</strong>: K\u1e5b\u1e63\u1e47a, the Buddha, Kalki, the great philosophical schools, the modern moment.<br><br>I write these in the order they ask to be written, not the order the timeline runs. <em>Sometimes the avatar I expect to be next is not what wants to be built that morning. The work has its own intelligence about sequence.</em> -RR`
