    'No. You are eternally distinct from God. Merger with God is not liberation — it would mean the annihilation of your reality. The very idea of "you are Brahman" is the most dangerous philosophical error. Madhva called Advaita "the gateway to nihilism."',
    'Mokṣa is eternal beatific proximity to Viṣṇu — ānanda-tāratamya — but the hierarchy among liberated souls is preserved even in liberation. Different souls experience different degrees of bliss eternally. The self\'s individuality is never dissolved.',
