    'The soul is a part of Brahman — tat-tadaṃśa — a real, distinct ray of Kṛṣṇa\'s own light. Not identical, not completely separate. The soul is Kṛṣṇa\'s own self, extended. The relationship is one of love between the whole and a real part of itself.',
