// CHAPTER VIII — BREATH OF THE UNIVERSE (analysis of the uploaded chart)
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TB_CONTENT.breath = `
<div class="tb-eyebrow">Chapter VIII · the same pattern, every scale</div>
<h2 class="tb-h">Breath of the Universe — the geometry of energy flow within</h2>

<p class="tb-sk">यथा पिण्डे तथा ब्रह्माण्डे, यथा ब्रह्माण्डे तथा पिण्डे।<br>
<em class="tb-sk-tr">yathā piṇḍe tathā brahmāṇḍe, yathā brahmāṇḍe tathā piṇḍe</em> ·
<em class="tb-sk-en">as it is in the body, so it is in the cosmos · as it is in the cosmos, so it is in the body.</em></p>

<p>There is one shape that energy makes when energy is allowed to move freely. <em>One.</em> An atom draws it. An apple holds its seeds inside it. A magnet's field traces it. A water vortex collapses through it. A hurricane spins on it. A galaxy unfurls along it. The iris of an eye opens around it. The human heart pumps through it. The earth's magnetosphere is one. So is the human aura. <strong>One geometry. Sixteen different resolutions.</strong></p>

<p class="tb-pull">The body you are walking around in is doing nothing more, and nothing less, than what the galaxy is doing — only at a different scale.</p>

<h3 class="tb-sub">Three claims, one geometry</h3>

<ol class="tb-list">
  <li><strong>The torus is the geometry of self-sustaining flow.</strong> A pattern that pumps energy out the top, lets it fall around the sides, draws it back in through the bottom, and pushes it back up through the centre — perpetually, with no leakage. This is the only known geometry that can do this without an external power source. Engineers call it a <em>self-sustaining vortex</em>; biologists call it a <em>homeostatic system</em>; the Upaniṣads call it a <em>prāṇic field</em>. They are describing one structure.</li>
  <li><strong>Vector equilibrium is the seed.</strong> The dimensionless point at the centre — <em>bindu</em> in Sanskrit, <em>vector equilibrium</em> in modern geometry — is where all forces are perfectly balanced. From this point of balance, every torus blooms outward. The Vedic term and the modern term describe the same locus. <em>Same idea, different vocabulary, identical diagram.</em></li>
  <li><strong>Every living and elemental form on earth is a torus.</strong> The apple's seed-cavity, the magnet's field, the water vortex, the hurricane, the galaxy, the eye, the heart's pulse, the human aura — these are not <em>analogous</em> to one another. They are <em>literally</em> the same geometry, observed at different scales. <em>The body is not "like" a galaxy. The body is a galaxy at a smaller resolution.</em></li>
</ol>

<h3 class="tb-sub">The same shape, nine times</h3>

<p>Below are nine of these forms, each drawn live in motion. <em>Watch them long enough and the pattern becomes undeniable.</em> The torus does not care what it is made of. Plasma, water, blood, light, mind — it shapes them all the same way.</p>

<div class="tb-bou-grid">
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="atom"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Atom · electron shells</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="apple"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Apple · seed cavity</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="magnet"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Bar magnet · field lines</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="vortex"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Water vortex</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="hurricane"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Hurricane · from above</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="galaxy"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Spiral galaxy</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="heart"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Heart · field pulse</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="eye"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Iris · radial fibres</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tb-bou-cell">
    <canvas class="tb-bou-canvas" data-kind="earth"></canvas>
    <div class="tb-bou-cap">Earth · magnetosphere</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h3 class="tb-sub">Why this matters for sādhanā</h3>

<p>If the geometry of energy flow is the same at every scale, then <strong>working with one scale is working with all of them.</strong> When you settle the breath, you are not just settling <em>your</em> breath. You are settling the same pattern that the galaxy is using to hold itself together. <em>This is not a metaphor. The mathematics is the same.</em> When the Upaniṣads say <em>"yathā piṇḍe, tathā brahmāṇḍe"</em> — as in the body, so in the cosmos — they are not speaking poetically. They are stating a structural fact.</p>

<p>A galaxy is not a thing that has a torus around it. A galaxy <em>is</em> the torus, made visible by what happens to be in the path of the spinning. So is your body. <em>The flow does not have them. They are the flow.</em></p>

<h3 class="tb-sub">The lived implication</h3>

<p>When you stand still and feel the field around you — not imagine it, <em>feel</em> it — what you are feeling is the same shape that the earth is making, and that the sun is making, and that the local cluster of galaxies is making. <strong>You are not nested inside it. You are it, in miniature.</strong> The miniature is not a smaller version. The miniature is the full thing, reduced in size only because that is the resolution at which it can carry a name and walk around.</p>

<p><em>The torus does not surround you. The torus is you.</em> What we call "the universe" is the same torus, only larger. To meditate is to remember this — not to learn it. There is nothing to learn. There is only what to stop forgetting.</p>

<p class="tb-source">— Cross-references · Atharvaveda 10.7 (Skambha as the cosmic pillar) · Praśna Upaniṣad 3 (the five winds) · Śiva Saṃhitā 2.13–2.31 · Brihadāraṇyaka Upaniṣad 2.5 (the honey doctrine) · Buckminster Fuller on vector equilibrium · Randolph Stone, Polarity Therapy. Original synthesis by Rahul S.</p>
`;

