      makeSection('ॐ','A-U-M','Three Sounds, One Reality','The entire universe in a single syllable.',
        '<strong>A</strong> — arises from the back of the throat, the widest opening. Represents the waking state (Jagrat), creation, Brahma. <strong>U</strong> — moves to the mid-palate. Represents the dream state (Svapna), preservation, Vishnu. <strong>M</strong> — closes at the lips. Represents deep sleep (Sushupti), dissolution, Shiva. The <strong>silence after M</strong> — that is Turiya, the fourth state, Brahman itself. The Mandukya Upanishad says: <em>OM is everything. Past, present, future — all is OM. Whatever transcends time — that too is OM.</em>',
        ['Om (Aum)','Turiya','Jagrat','Svapna','Sushupti'])+
      makeSection('∿','The Cosmic Microwave Background','The Universe\'s OM','380,000 years after the Big Bang, the universe sang.',
        'The Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB) radiation — discovered in 1964 — is the afterglow of the Big Bang: the first light released as the universe cooled. It carries within it <strong>sound waves from the early universe</strong> — acoustic oscillations that shaped the distribution of all subsequent matter. Cosmologists literally listen to these patterns. <em>The universe began with a sound.</em> The Vedic tradition calls this the Anahata Nada — the unstruck sound. Modern physics calls it the CMB acoustic peaks. The ancient and the cutting-edge describe the same phenomenon.',
        ['Praṇava','Brahman','Sphoṭa']);
