        '<strong>Vaikhari</strong> — audible, spoken sound. The words you hear. <strong>Madhyama</strong> — mental sound. The voice in your head. <strong>Pashyanti</strong> — visionary sound. The level where sound becomes light, where mantras reveal their visual form. <strong>Para</strong> — transcendent sound. Beyond all vibration. The silence that is the source of all sound. <em>Nada Yoga is the practice of following sound inward</em> — from external hearing to internal listening to the perception of subtle vibrations to the silence at the source.',
